# PowerShell must reach Windows byte-for-byte. Windows PowerShell 5.1 reads a
# BOM-less file as the system ANSI codepage, so a UTF-8 BOM is load-bearing —
# without it a stray multi-byte sequence becomes mojibake mid-token and the
# script fails to parse. `-text` disables line-ending normalisation so the BOM
# and the CRLFs survive a checkout on any platform.
# The scripts themselves are unmaintained (the target is Linux/WSL2); this only
# guarantees that what is in the repo still parses. See tests/test_platform.py.
*.ps1 -text
assets/marker/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
assets/ballpoint/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
assets/grease-pencil/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
assets/cut-paper/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
assets/light/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
